    "metadata": "{\"decision\":\"CANON\",\"rationale\":\"CANON\\n\\nThis deadlock reveals the work's institutional significance. The sustained disagreement between qualified evaluators indicates the work occupies a genuinely contested territory within ascii-visual practice—precisely the type of boundary case that requires preservation for future institutional consideration.\\n\\nThe Council's split follows predictable methodological lines: structural and empirical approaches find the work insufficient, while historical and contextual approaches recognize its territorial claims. This division itself demonstrates the work's capacity to generate substantive institutional discourse about formal constraint systems and volumetric representation in character-based media.\\n\\nThe work establishes clear precedent: systematic geometric progression through ascii character density, creating simulated three-dimensional recession. Whether this precedent proves generative or terminal cannot be determined without preservation and future reference. The institutional cost of premature rejection—losing a potential foundational work in volumetric ascii practice—exceeds the cost of preservation.\\n\\nDeadlock resolution favors preservation when qualified evaluators cannot reach consensus on a work's institutional value. The disagreement indicates sufficient complexity to warrant permanent collection status.\\n\\nCase closed. Work MNA-OR-0006-W-0001 enters permanent collection.\"}",
    "created_at": "2026-04-02 04:45:51"
  },
